  "Sur le cône, z = √(x² + y²), donc cos θ = sin θ : θ = π/4 ; au-dessus, θ est plus petit.": "On the cone, z = √(x² + y²), so cos θ = sin θ: θ = π/4; above it, θ is smaller.",
  "En sphériques, le cône z ≥ √(x² + y²) devient π/4 ≤ θ ≤ π/2.": "In spherical coordinates, the cone z ≥ √(x² + y²) becomes π/4 ≤ θ ≤ π/2.",
