  "Solution unique sur |t| ≤ h, avec h = min(a, b/K) :": "Unique solution on |t| ≤ h, with h = min(a, b/K):",
  "Problème de Cauchy y′ = f(t, y) = {f}, y(0) = {y0} sur le rectangle R : {R} (donc |y| ≤ {B}). Trouve une constante de Lipschitz M, une borne K de |f| et l'intervalle |t| ≤ h où la solution existe et est unique.": "Cauchy problem y′ = f(t, y) = {f}, y(0) = {y0} on the rectangle R: {R} (so |y| ≤ {B}). Find a Lipschitz constant M, a bound K of |f| and the interval |t| ≤ h on which the solution exists and is unique.",
  "Problème de Cauchy y′ = f(t, y) = {f}, y(0) = {y0} sur le rectangle R : {R}. Trouve une constante de Lipschitz M, une borne K de |f| et l'intervalle |t| ≤ h où la solution existe et est unique.": "Cauchy problem y′ = f(t, y) = {f}, y(0) = {y0} on the rectangle R: {R}. Find a Lipschitz constant M, a bound K of |f| and the interval |t| ≤ h on which the solution exists and is unique.",
  "Lipschitz : majore |∂f/∂y| sur R. Intervalle : min(a, b/K).": "Lipschitz: bound |∂f/∂y| on R. Interval: min(a, b/K).",
  "Sur R : {why}. Par exemple |∂f/∂y| ≤ {m}.": "On R: {why}. For example |∂f/∂y| ≤ {m}.",
  "Si f est continue et bornée sur ℝ, le problème y′ = f(t), y(t₀) = y₀ a une unique solution.": "If f is continuous and bounded on ℝ, the problem y′ = f(t), y(t₀) = y₀ has a unique solution.",
  "Vrai : on intègre, y(t) = y₀ + ∫ de t₀ à t de f(s) ds, et deux solutions ont la même dérivée et la même valeur en t₀.": "True: integrate, y(t) = y₀ + ∫ from t₀ to t of f(s) ds, and two solutions have the same derivative and the same value at t₀.",
  "Si f est continue et bornée, le problème y′ = f(y), y(0) = 0 a une unique solution locale.": "If f is continuous and bounded, the problem y′ = f(y), y(0) = 0 has a unique local solution.",
  "Faux : y′ = 3y^(2/3) (tronquée pour être bornée) a les solutions y = 0 et y = t³. La continuité ne donne que l'existence ; l'unicité demande f Lipschitz en y.": "False: y′ = 3y^(2/3) (truncated to be bounded) has the solutions y = 0 and y = t³. Continuity only gives existence; uniqueness needs f Lipschitz in y.",
  "Pour y′ = 3y^(2/3), y(0) = 0 : y₁(t) =": "For y′ = 3y^(2/3), y(0) = 0: y₁(t) =",
  "Si f est continue, le problème y′ = f(y), y(0) = 0 a une unique solution sur [0 ; 1].": "If f is continuous, the problem y′ = f(y), y(0) = 0 has a unique solution on [0 ; 1].",
  "Faux : y′ = 2√|y| a les solutions y = 0 et y = t² sur [0 ; 1]. √|y| n'est pas Lipschitz près de 0.": "False: y′ = 2√|y| has the solutions y = 0 and y = t² on [0 ; 1]. √|y| is not Lipschitz near 0.",
  "Pour y′ = 2√|y|, y(0) = 0 : y₁(t) =": "For y′ = 2√|y|, y(0) = 0: y₁(t) =",
  "Si f ∈ C¹(ℝ²), le problème y′ = f(t, y), y(t₀) = y₀ a une unique solution locale.": "If f ∈ C¹(ℝ²), the problem y′ = f(t, y), y(t₀) = y₀ has a unique local solution.",
  "Vrai : ∂f/∂y est continue, donc bornée sur un rectangle autour de (t₀, y₀) : f est Lipschitz en y, et le théorème s'applique.": "True: ∂f/∂y is continuous, hence bounded on a rectangle around (t₀, y₀): f is Lipschitz in y, and the theorem applies.",
  "Si f ∈ C¹(ℝ²), la solution de y′ = f(t, y), y(0) = 1 est définie pour tout t ∈ ℝ.": "If f ∈ C¹(ℝ²), the solution of y′ = f(t, y), y(0) = 1 is defined for every t ∈ ℝ.",
  "Faux : y′ = y², y(0) = 1 donne y = 1/(1 − t), qui explose en t = 1. Le théorème est local.": "False: y′ = y², y(0) = 1 gives y = 1/(1 − t), which blows up at t = 1. The theorem is local.",
  "L'équation y‴ = f(t, y, y′, y″) demande trois conditions initiales, y(t₀), y′(t₀) et y″(t₀), pour une solution unique.": "The equation y‴ = f(t, y, y′, y″) needs three initial conditions, y(t₀), y′(t₀) and y″(t₀), for a unique solution.",
  "Vrai : on la ramène au système d'ordre 1 en (y, y′, y″), qui a trois inconnues, donc trois conditions initiales.": "True: it reduces to the first-order system in (y, y′, y″), which has three unknowns, hence three initial conditions.",
  "Si f est continue sur ℝ², le problème y′ = f(t, y), y(t₀) = y₀ a au moins une solution locale.": "If f is continuous on ℝ², the problem y′ = f(t, y), y(t₀) = y₀ has at least one local solution.",
  "Vrai : c'est le théorème d'existence (Peano). L'unicité, elle, demande plus.": "True: it is the existence theorem (Peano). Uniqueness needs more.",
  "Existence : f continue. Unicité locale : f Lipschitz en y. Rien de global.": "Existence: f continuous. Local uniqueness: f Lipschitz in y. Nothing global.",
  "Pense à y′ = 3y^(2/3) (deux solutions) et à y′ = y² (explosion).": "Think of y′ = 3y^(2/3) (two solutions) and of y′ = y² (blow-up).",
  "L'énoncé est vrai.": "The statement is true.",
